{# TM·B — GROUPED BY TIER.

   Three bands, in the order the enum declares them. The top two are the ESCAPE
   HATCHES — they pass every permission check without holding a position — and
   everybody else is in the third.

   THIS DIRECTION CAN NO LONGER ANSWER ITS OWN QUESTION FROM THE BANDS ALONE,
   and it says so rather than hiding it. Administering the team is the
   team.manage permission now, so a Staff member can hold it. Every person who
   does is marked, wherever they sit.

   The whole roster, not a page of it: a banded list whose bands are cut in half
   by a pager is a list that lies about its bands. #}
{% import '@UhifadhiTeam/team/_bits.html.twig' as bits %}

<div class="c" data-tm data-tm-dir="b">
    <span class="tab">Roster<span class="src">&middot; grouped by tier</span></span>

    <p class="use" style="margin:2px 0 14px">Three bands, in the order the enum declares them. The top two are the
    <b>escape hatches</b> &mdash; they pass every permission check without holding a position &mdash; and everybody
    else is in the third. <b>This direction can no longer answer its own question from the bands alone</b>, and
    says so rather than hiding it: administering the team is the <span class="mono">team.manage</span> permission
    now, so a Staff member can hold it. Every person who does is marked, wherever they sit.</p>

    {# THE POST-RULING WEAKNESS, said plainly rather than apologised for. Both
       halves are true and the direction is worth keeping for the second. #}
    <div class="tm-correct" style="margin:0 0 16px;border-top:0;padding-top:0">
        {{ bits.icon_info() }}
        <div><b>As a grouping this now sorts {{ tierCounts['super_admin'] }} + {{ tierCounts['admin'] }} + {{ tierCounts['staff'] }}.</b>
        With three system tiers and two of them escape hatches, almost everybody lands in one enormous Staff band,
        and a band holding most of the roster is not doing much sorting. <b>That is the honest cost, and it is not
        the whole story:</b> this is still the fastest screen in the product for seeing <b>who stands above the
        matrix</b> &mdash; the accounts whose authority no permission grants and no permission can take away. If
        you want the roster sorted rather than that question answered, take <b>The org chart</b> instead.</div>
    </div>

    <div class="tm-scroll">
        <table class="tbl">
            <thead><tr><th>Person</th><th>Position</th><th>Ranger code</th><th>Account</th><th></th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
                {% for tier in tiers %}
                    {% set band = everybody|filter(p => p.teamRole == tier) %}
                    {% if band|length %}
                        {% set managers = band|filter(p => p.position and p.position.hasPermissionValue('team.manage')) %}
                        <tr class="tm-bandrow"><td colspan="5"><div class="tm-band">
                            {{ bits.tier_pill(tier) }}<b>{{ band|length }} {{ band|length == 1 ? 'person' : 'people' }}</b>
                            <span class="say">{{ tier.grants }}</span>
                            {% if managers|length %}
                                <span class="gr"><span class="tm-mgr">{{ bits.icon_shield() }}{{ managers|length }} hold team.manage</span></span>
                            {% endif %}
                        </div></td></tr>
                        {% for person in band %}
                            <tr class="tm-memrow{{ person.isActive ? '' : ' tm-off' }}{{ person.position is null and not person.teamRole.canManageContent ? ' loose' : '' }}">
                                <td class="tm-in">{{ bits.person(person, person == app.user) }}</td>
                                <td>{{ bits.position_cell(person, path('team_positions')) }}</td>
                                <td>{{ bits.ranger_code(person) }}</td>
                                <td>{{ bits.account_cell(person) }}</td>
                                <td class="tm-acts">{{ bits.open_button(person) }}</td>
                            </tr>
                        {% endfor %}
                    {% endif %}
                {% endfor %}
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>
</div>
